# A .vercelignore replaces .gitignore for upload filtering, so anything the
# web build does not need has to be listed here even if git already ignores it.

# Rendered video output. @continuum/video stays a workspace member so the
# lockfile still resolves, but its media never reaches the web deployment —
# out/segments/hook.mov alone is 107MB, past Vercel's 100MB per-file limit.
apps/video/out
apps/video/build
apps/video/assets

# Screenshot dumps kept for review history; 53MB the build never reads.
docs/audit-screenshots
docs/screenshots
docs/hackathon

# Agent worktrees. `.gitignore` already excludes them, but `.vercelignore`
# replaces `.gitignore` for upload filtering — and an agent writing Playwright
# artifacts into one mid-upload makes the deploy fail with ENOENT on a file
# that existed when the file list was built.
.claude
